// `sortOpenapi.paths: "tags"` orders the `paths` object by each path item's tag key.
//
// The JSON twin of the YAML backend's `paths-tags` fixture, and it must produce the same order.
//
// The tag key is the first tag of the first method present in
// `[get, query, post, put, delete, patch, options, head]` with a non-empty `tags`:
//
// `/two-methods` keys on `zebra` from its `post`, not `alpha` from its `patch` -- `post` comes earlier
//   in that list, and the list order is upstream's, not the source's.
// `/first-tag-only` keys on `beta`, not `aardvark`: only the first tag counts.
// `/untagged` and `/no-methods` key on the empty string, which sorts before every real tag, and their
//   tie keeps source order.
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "paths": {
    "/two-methods": {
      "patch": { "tags": ["alpha"], "responses": {} },
      "post": { "tags": ["zebra"], "responses": {} }
    },
    "/first-tag-only": { "get": { "tags": ["beta", "aardvark"], "responses": {} } },
    "/untagged": { "get": { "responses": {} } },
    "/no-methods": { "description": "not an operation" }
  }
}
